<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Recluster · {{ spec.name }}</title>
<style>
:root { --ink:#1b1b1b; --muted:#5f5e58; --rule:#d8d6cf; --bg:#fbfaf7; --panel:#ffffff; --soft:#f3f1ea;
        --accent:#1f4e79; --pass:#2f6b3a; --fail:#9b3b2e; --warn:#8a6a1e; }
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body { margin:0; background:var(--bg); color:var(--ink);
       font: 15px/1.55 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; }
main { max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 36px 24px 72px; }
.mono, code, td.num, .params { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
.eyebrow { font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 10px; }
h1 { font-size: 27px; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 0 0 6px; }
.sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 22px; }
h2 { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 650; margin: 44px 0 12px; padding-bottom: 6px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
h3 { font-size: 14.5px; font-weight: 650; margin: 22px 0 8px; color: var(--muted); }
p { margin: 8px 0; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 14px; background: var(--panel); }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); vertical-align: top; }
th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; background: var(--soft); }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; }
.verdict { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 18px 0 6px; }
.badge { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; padding: 12px 18px; border: 2px solid; border-radius: 4px;
         font-weight: 750; font-size: 20px; letter-spacing: .03em; background: var(--panel); }
.badge .icon { font-size: 22px; line-height: 1; }
.badge.robust { border-color: var(--pass); color: var(--pass); }
.badge.fragile { border-color: var(--warn); color: var(--warn); border-style: dashed; }
.badge.not-supported { border-color: var(--fail); color: var(--fail); }
.badge.neutral { border-color: var(--rule); color: var(--muted); }
.badge.small-badge { font-size: 15px; padding: 8px 12px; }
.verdict-text { flex: 1 1 420px; }
.kv { display:grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 3px 18px; margin: 10px 0; font-size: 14px; }
.kv dt { color: var(--muted); } .kv dd { margin: 0; }
.note { background: var(--panel); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding: 10px 14px; margin: 14px 0; font-size: 14px; }
.note.flag { border-left-color: var(--fail); }
.pass::before { content: "✓ "; color: var(--pass); font-weight: 700; }
.fail::before { content: "✕ "; color: var(--fail); font-weight: 700; }
.na { color: var(--muted); }
details { margin-top: 10px; }
summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent); }
pre { background: var(--soft); padding: 12px 14px; font-size: 12.5px; overflow: auto; max-height: 520px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.legend { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 6px; }
.small { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
svg { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
footer { margin-top: 56px; padding-top: 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
.llm { border: 1px dashed var(--rule); padding: 10px 14px; margin: 14px 0; background: var(--soft); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<div class="eyebrow">Recluster report · {{ spec.claim_type.replace('_', ' ') }} · {{ mode }} mode</div>
<h1>{{ spec.name }}</h1>
<p class="sub">{{ data.path_name }} · {{ data.n_cells | thousands }} cells × {{ data.n_genes | thousands }} genes · counts from <span class="mono">{{ data.counts_source }}</span></p>

<div class="verdict">
  <div class="badge {{ verdict.label | lower | replace(' ', '-') }}"><span class="icon">{{ verdict_icon }}</span>{{ verdict.label }}</div>
  <div class="verdict-text">
    <p>{{ verdict.summary }}</p>
    <dl class="kv">
      <dt>Survival</dt><dd class="mono">{{ verdict.n_holds }} / {{ verdict.n_runs }} runs ({{ (100 * verdict.survival) | round(0) | int }}%)</dd>
      {% if verdict.recovered_survival is not none and spec.claim_type == 'population_exists' %}
      <dt>Recovered as a cluster</dt><dd class="mono">{{ (100 * verdict.recovered_survival) | round(0) | int }}% of runs (before the replicate check)</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if verdict.cell_level_survival is not none and spec.claim_type != 'population_exists' %}
      <dt>Naive cell-level</dt><dd class="mono">{{ (100 * verdict.cell_level_survival) | round(0) | int }}% of runs (not used for the verdict)</dd>
      {% endif %}
      <dt>Rule</dt><dd>ROBUST ≥ {{ (100 * thresholds.robust_min_survival) | int }}% · FRAGILE ≥ {{ (100 * thresholds.fragile_min_survival) | int }}% · else NOT SUPPORTED</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</div>
{% if verdict.pseudoreplication_flag %}
<div class="note flag"><strong>Pseudoreplication flag.</strong> Cell-level statistics support the claim in {{ (100 * verdict.cell_level_survival) | round(0) | int }}% of runs, but replicate-aware statistics support it in only {{ (100 * verdict.survival) | round(0) | int }}%. Treating cells as independent replicates inflates significance (Squair et al., <em>Nat Commun</em> 2021;12:5692).</div>
{% endif %}
{% if llm_summary %}
<div class="llm"><div class="eyebrow">LLM summary of computed results</div>{{ llm_summary }}</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>Claim</h2>
<pre class="mono">{{ spec_yaml }}</pre>
<p class="small">Reference cell set: {{ reference_source }}.</p>

<h2>Survival across the grid</h2>
<p class="small">One square per run in grid order; the thick-bordered square is the baseline. Hover for the run's settings.</p>
{{ run_strip | safe }}
<h3>By analysis choice</h3>
<p class="small">Fraction of runs with that setting in which the claim held. ● marks the baseline value. Hatched = failed.</p>
{{ by_choice_chart | safe }}

<h2>What broke it</h2>
{% if verdict.oat_flips %}
<p>One-at-a-time changes from baseline that {{ 'broke' if verdict.baseline_holds else 'rescued' }} the claim:</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Change</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for f in verdict.oat_flips %}<tr><td class="params">{{ f.params_changed | params }}</td><td><span class="{{ 'pass' if f.holds else 'fail' }}">{{ 'held' if f.holds else 'failed' }}</span></td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
{% else %}
<p>No single one-at-a-time change flipped the baseline result.</p>
{% endif %}
{% if verdict.breakers %}
<h3>Failure rate by setting</h3>
<table><thead><tr><th>Axis</th><th>Value</th><th class="num">Runs</th><th class="num">Failed</th><th class="num">Fail rate</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for b in verdict.breakers %}<tr><td class="mono">{{ b.axis }}</td><td class="mono">{{ b.value | fmtval }}{% if b.is_baseline %} ●{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ b.n_runs }}</td><td class="num">{{ b.n_runs - b.n_holds }}</td><td class="num">{{ (100 * (b.n_runs - b.n_holds) / b.n_runs) | round(0) | int }}%</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
{% else %}
<p>The claim held in every run; no setting is associated with failure.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Replicate-aware vs cell-level</h2>
{{ comparison_html | safe }}

<h2>Time-of-day check</h2>
{{ time_html | safe }}

{% if as_labelled %}
<h2>As labelled</h2>
<p class="small">The same test applied to the cells exactly as labelled in <span class="mono">{{ spec.columns.labels }}</span> = <span class="mono">{{ spec.target.label_value }}</span>, without re-clustering. This is the claim as the original analysis made it.</p>
{{ as_labelled_html | safe }}
{% endif %}

<h2>All runs</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Settings (differences from baseline)</th><th class="num">Cells</th><th class="num">Clusters</th><th>Population</th>{% for k in key_stat_names %}<th class="num">{{ k }}</th>{% endfor %}<th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in runs %}<tr>
<td class="num">{{ r.index }}</td>
<td class="params">{{ r.label }}</td>
<td class="num">{{ r.n_cells | thousands }}</td>
<td class="num">{{ r.n_clusters }}</td>
<td class="mono" style="white-space:nowrap">{{ r.match.n_cells }} cells{% if r.match.clusters %} / {{ r.match.clusters | length }} cl.{% endif %}</td>
{% for k in key_stat_names %}<td class="num">{{ r.key_stats[k] | fmtnum }}</td>{% endfor %}
<td><span class="{{ 'pass' if r.holds else 'fail' }}">{{ 'held' if r.holds else 'failed' }}</span>{% if r.details.reasons %}<div class="small">{{ r.details.reasons | join('; ') }}</div>{% endif %}{% if r.warnings %}<div class="small">⚠ {{ r.warnings | join('; ') }}</div>{% endif %}</td>
</tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>

<h2>Methods</h2>
<p>{{ methods }}</p>
<p class="small">This paragraph is generated from a fixed template filled with the settings used. It is not written by a language model.</p>

<h2>Thresholds</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for k, v in thresholds.model_dump().items() %}<tr><td class="mono">{{ k }}</td><td class="mono">{{ v }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
<p class="small"><span class="mono">doublet_residual_ratio_max</span> and <span class="mono">doublet_libsize_ratio_min</span> are informational: they only label the cluster-level doublet check, and no verdict depends on them.</p>
<p class="small">Doublet-population removal (grid setting): {% if grid.doublet_cluster_removal %}on in runs with doublet removal on; a cluster is removed when its AUROC against simulated doublets is below <span class="mono">doublet_cluster_auroc_max</span> = <span class="mono">{{ grid.doublet_cluster_auroc_max }}</span>{% else %}off (<span class="mono">doublet_cluster_removal</span> = false){% endif %}.</p>

<h2>Provenance</h2>
<dl class="kv">
  <dt>Input</dt><dd class="mono">{{ data.path }}</dd>
  <dt>SHA-256</dt><dd class="mono">{{ data.sha256 }}</dd>
  <dt>Recluster</dt><dd class="mono">{{ provenance.environment.packages.recluster }}</dd>
  <dt>Python</dt><dd class="mono">{{ provenance.environment.python }} · {{ provenance.environment.platform }}</dd>
  <dt>Key packages</dt><dd class="mono">scanpy {{ provenance.environment.packages.scanpy }} · anndata {{ provenance.environment.packages.anndata }} · pydeseq2 {{ provenance.environment.packages.pydeseq2 }} · harmonypy {{ provenance.environment.packages.harmonypy }}</dd>
  <dt>Started</dt><dd class="mono">{{ provenance.started_at }}</dd>
  <dt>Total runtime</dt><dd class="mono">{{ total_runtime_s | round(1) }} s</dd>
</dl>
<details><summary>Full provenance log (JSON)</summary><pre class="mono">{{ provenance_json }}</pre></details>

<footer>Recluster {{ provenance.environment.packages.recluster }} · an independent stress test for single-cell RNA-seq claims · all numbers in this report were computed by deterministic code.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
